 **A-01 | Blocker | STORE.** Evidence: audit/chain.py:216 `"""Never raises: the chain, then the outbox table, then memory (all drained by reconcile)."""`; audit/protocol.py:27 `def reconcile(self) -> int:` "Drain the outbox"; runtime/tick.py:249-253 STEPS = sweep, reconcile (the approvals one, tick.py:85), stuck, checkpoint, purge_evidence ... no audit step; `grep -rn "\.reconcile()" src` finds no call outside tests (tests/test_cuj.py:202, tests/warden_port/test_audit_chain.py:514). Wrong: when the chain (or folder) cannot be written, `write_outcome` parks the event in `audit_outbox` or in memory (chain.py:215-231, local_dir.py:110-124) and returns None. Nothing in production writes it back. Parked events include the result of an executed action and approval decisions (agent_loop.py `_note(run,"action","result")`). No log line on the fallback (no `_LOG` call in those blocks). Memory-parked events are lost at restart. `verify` only checks rows that exist, so the gap is invisible. Fix: tick step `audit_reconcile` calling `app.audit.reconcile()` and logging the count; warn (class only) at the fallback; test: fail a write, run tick, event appears in `audit.events()`. Verdict FIX-NEEDED; own NEEDED. Guarantee chain.py:216 and protocol.py:27-29; code none in production; test only manual calls (test_audit_chain.py:505-518).
