 **A-03 | Major | SECURITY.** Evidence: runtime/agent_loop.py:760 `def execute(self, run_id: str, approval: Any = None)`; actions/executor.py:111-114 only checks `approval is None or approval.decision != "approve"`; runtime/runs.py:14-16 PLAN_READY may go to EXECUTING. Wrong: approval is proved by an argument; `Runtime.execute` never reads the stored approval request. Code inside the service that passes a hand-made `ApprovalDecision(decision="approve", plan_hash=<hash>)` runs a needs-approval plan with no person approving. Agents do not hold this call; in-process only (exploit UNVERIFIED). In pilot/prod no executor exists (app.py:173, deferred.py:55), so today it matters in dev only, but the binding is the guarantee. Fix: in `Runtime.execute`, for needs_approval load `store.get_approval_request`, require APPROVED with matching plan hash and stored decision; ignore the argument; add a forged-decision negative test (tests/test_executor.py:78 tests only the None case). FIX-NEEDED; NEEDED.
